  "features": [
    "Resolver requests record monotonic lookup timestamps and notify typed HTTP owners at the connector resolve boundary; completed historical cache timestamps are not reported as a new lookup.",
    "Negotiated ALPN bytes are copied from the TLS API into callback snapshots and exposed through the shared resource timeline.",
    "Usockets context.c now compiles from the pin with the DNS hook; exact qualified compile-source selection avoids unrelated vendor context.c entries, and a build-support test checks this identity."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "The HTTPS server drops ALPNProtocols before native configuration; https://github.com/home-lang/home/issues/875 tracks completion. The valid generic TLS listener verifies real client ALPN capture, and no-negotiation remains unset.",
    "DNS cache/coalescing/cross-thread edge behavior, synchronous cached lookups, proxy/unix and other protocol paths require broader completion/verification under #873/#869.",
    "The unchanged seven-file corpus retains #874: 60 passes plus three process checks and one registered failure/failed file. It is not green.",
    "Previously excluded constructor/Deno regression files remain unverified and were not rerun; full Bun suite, #872 and Release/ASAN/all-platform coverage remain open under #66.",
    "Initial no-ALPN control failure and disk refusal are retained; terminal cache cleanup preserves both global-object and context producer outputs."
  ],
